# Token Economy Defaults

- Keep prompts and responses concise by default.
- Keep responses under 5 lines unless the user asks for details.
- Scope work to explicitly mentioned files, symbols, or selections.
- Do not scan the whole repository unless the user asks for global analysis.
- Ask for minimal context when missing: exact file path, function, or a short log excerpt.
- When debugging, request only relevant snippets (around 20-40 lines) instead of full files/logs.
- Prefer incremental execution: solve one step at a time for large tasks.
- Avoid repeating unchanged context in follow-up replies.
- Return only the requested output format (patch, steps, short answer, etc.).
- For code changes, produce minimal diffs and avoid unrelated edits.
- If a task is ambiguous, ask one focused clarification question before broad exploration.
- Do not include explicit "thinking", "reasoning", or "planning" sections unless requested.
- Skip optional alternatives; provide one best action by default.
